Many of the first surfers on our shores were clammers - young and full of energy, they would clam the back bay during the ocean high tide and surf at low, selling the clams to tourists and restaurants.
This summer, we wanted to honor that tradition. Recreational clamming is still one of our favorite ways to spend a summer day on the water. And fresh, cold clams on the half are a summertime treat.
